title: Relax harder
---

<div class="page mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <section class="grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] md:gap-14">
    <div>
      <h1 class="page-title mb-8 mt-0">Relax harder.</h1>
      <p class="mb-10 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-slate-100 sm:text-2xl">We train one thing: staying calm and relaxed inside your own head.</p>

      <p class="page-prose mb-6">When I started freediving, I thought it was about swimming. It turned out to be training in staying calm. On days I could not relax, I could not dive.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-6">Underwater you cannot fake calm. Go down tense or upset and your air runs out at once. Go down relaxed and the same breath lasts far longer.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">So in every session, in the pool and on the line, we practise letting go until depth feels like home. The best dive is the one where you do not think at all.</p>
    </div>
    <img src="/images/nick.webp" alt="Nick Ostrovsky, freediving instructor, on the boat before a depth session" width="1000" height="1500" class="home-about-photo">
  </section>

  <section class="mt-20 grid items-start gap-10 sm:mt-28 lg:grid-cols-[390px_1fr] lg:gap-14">
